<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Oswego</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Oswego was a British trading post and fort built in the 1720s at the mouth of the Oswego River on Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> State, to compete with the French for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a>. In August 1756 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-joseph-de-montcalm">Marquis de Montcalm</a> besieged and captured it with its garrison and destroyed it, one of the first major French successes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-oswego.jpg" alt="Fort Oswego" width="300" height="136" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:OswegoFort1727.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
